Section: Angle (base: arcsecond)

  Angle = unit family Arcsecond
    Arcsecond = 1
    Arcminute = 60
    Degree = 3600
    RightAngle = 324000
    FullCircle = 1296000
    Gradian = 3240

Section: ParticleEnergy (base: electron-volt)

 Energy at the quantum scale. 1 eV = 1.602e-19 joules -- far too
 small for the millijoule-based Energy family. Particle masses are
 expressed in eV/c^2 (proton ~ 938 MeV, electron ~ 0.511 MeV).

  ParticleEnergy = unit family ElectronVolt
    ElectronVolt = 1
    KeV = 1000
    MeV = 1000000
    GeV = 1000000000
    TeV = 1000000000000

Section: CrossSection (base: millibarn)

 Nuclear and particle interaction cross-sections. A "barn" is
 10^-24 cm^2 -- enormous by nuclear standards, hence the name.
 Typical values: thermal neutron capture ~ 1-1000 barns,
 neutrino scattering ~ femtobarns.

  CrossSection = unit family Microbarn
    Femtobarn = 1
    Picobarn = 1000
    Nanobarn = 1000000
    Microbarn = 1000000000
    Millibarn = 1000000000000
    Barn = 1000000000000000
    Kilobarn = 1000000000000000000

Section: NeutronFlux (base: n/cm^2/s, stored as integer)

 Neutron flux intensity. Thermal reactors ~ 10^13 n/cm^2/s,
 fast reactors ~ 10^15. Fluence (time-integrated flux) is
 neutrons/cm^2.

  NeutronFlux = unit Integer
  Fluence = unit Integer

Section: RadiationDose (base: microsievert)

 Absorbed dose and dose equivalent. Gray measures energy deposited
 per kg of tissue. Sievert weights by radiation type (quality factor).
 1 Sv = 1 Gy for gamma/beta, 20 Gy for alpha.

  DoseEquivalent = unit family Microsievert
    Microsievert = 1
    Millisievert = 1000
    Sievert = 1000000

  AbsorbedDose = unit family Microgray
    Microgray = 1
    Milligray = 1000
    Gray = 1000000

Section: Radioactivity (base: becquerel)

 Decay rate. 1 Bq = 1 disintegration/second.
 1 Curie = 3.7e10 Bq (historical, from radium-226).

  Radioactivity = unit family Becquerel
    Becquerel = 1
    Kilobecquerel = 1000
    Megabecquerel = 1000000
    Gigabecquerel = 1000000000
    Curie = 37000000000

Section: MagneticField (base: microtesla)

 Earth's field ~ 25-65 microtesla. MRI magnets ~ 1.5-3 tesla.
 Gauss is CGS (1 T = 10,000 gauss).

  MagneticField = unit family Microtesla
    Microtesla = 1
    Millitesla = 1000
    Tesla = 1000000
    Gauss = 100

Section: Luminosity (base: lux)

  Illuminance = unit family Lux
    Lux = 1
    Kilolux = 1000
    FootCandle = 10

  LuminousFlux = unit family Lumen
    Lumen = 1
    Kilolumen = 1000

Section: Concentration (base: nanogram/liter, for clinical lab values)

 Blood chemistry, drug levels, toxicology. Clinical labs report in
 various units (mg/dL, mmol/L, ng/mL). Base is ng/L for resolution.

  Concentration = unit family NanogramPerLiter
    NanogramPerLiter = 1
    MicrogramPerLiter = 1000
    MilligramPerLiter = 1000000
    GramPerLiter = 1000000000
    NanogramPerML = 1000
    MicrogramPerDL = 10000
    MilligramPerDL = 10000000

Section: FlowRate (base: microliters/minute, for IV/infusion)

 IV drip rates, blood flow, ventilator volumes.

  FlowRate = unit family MicrolitPerMin
    MicrolitPerMin = 1
    MillilitPerMin = 1000
    LiterPerMin = 1000000
    MillilitPerHour = 16
    LiterPerHour = 16667

Section: BloodPressure (base: mmHg, the clinical standard)

  BloodPressure = unit family MmHg
    MmHg = 1
    BpKilopascal = 7

Section: DoseWeight (base: microgram, for drug dosing)

 Pharmacological dosing: mcg, mg, mg/kg.

  DoseWeight = unit family DoseMicrogram
    DoseMicrogram = 1
    DoseMilligram = 1000
    DoseGram = 1000000
    InternationalUnit = 1

Section: HeartRate (base: beats per minute)

  HeartRate = unit Integer

Section: BloodOxygen (base: percentage x10 for one decimal)

  SpO2 = unit Integer

Section: BodyTemperature (base: millidegree Celsius)

 Higher resolution than the integer Celsius in the Temperature
 section. 37000 = 37.0 C, 98600 = 98.6 F (after conversion).

  BodyTemp = unit family MilliCelsius
    MilliCelsius = 1
    DeciCelsius = 100
    CelsiusBody = 1000

  MilliCelsius-to-MilliFahrenheit : BodyTemp -> Integer
  MilliCelsius-to-MilliFahrenheit (mc) = mc * 9 / 5 + 32000

